  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "華人文化概論",
    "sub_ename": "INTRODUCTION TO CHINESE CULTURE",
    "describe_ch": "文化是人類歷史發展過程中創造的總成果，包括宗教、道德、藝術、科學等各方面，是一個族群的靈魂，也是傳承，更是累積而來的創造。「華」是中國的代稱，本課程的「華人」不僅限於漢族，同時包含部分被漢化的少數民族以及移居世界各地的華人，「華人文化」意謂具華人血統的族群文化。希望能經由認識華人文化，協助學生學習華語文，適應在台的學習生活。期能以流利的華語文比較族群文化差異，進而促進多元文化的交流，豐厚年輕學子的思想與觀點。",
    "describe_eh": "Culture is the result of human historical development. Culture includes religion, morality, art, science, etc. Culture is the soul and inheritance of a group of people, and it is also accumulated. \"Hua\" indicates China. Not only the Chinese are Han race, but also some ethnic minorities who have been Sinicized. Chinese culture means people with Chinese bloodlines, whether they are Chinese or not.\nWe hope to help students learn Chinese and adapt to study and life in Taiwan by understanding Chinese culture. Students can recognize ethnic cultural differences with fluent Chinese, thereby promoting multicultural exchanges and enriching the thoughts and perspectives of young students.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "1.認識華人社會的文化特色",
      "describe_en": "1. Understand the cultural characteristics of Chinese society"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "2.能以流利的華語文比較族群文化差異",
      "describe_en": "2. Able to recognize ethnic and cultural differences in Chinese"
    }
  ],
